 "body_text": "4 things every tracker on that list has in common — and the one thing Spotminders doesn't:\n\n1. They all go silent in the cargo hold.\nAirTag. Tile. Samsung. Ridge. Seven miles of air between your bag and the nearest relay. Not a glitch. Physics.\n\n2. They all fail the 45-minute transfer window.\nCDG. ORD. That's when bags get put on the wrong aircraft. That's the window every Bluetooth tracker cannot see.\n\n3. They were all designed for something else.\nKeys. Wallets. Coffee shops. Then repurposed for a cargo hold they were never built for.\n\n4. None of them are in the pilot's own bag.\nSpotminders is. Every deadhead flight. 60+ countries. Never flagged. Charged twice a year.\n\nThe passengers he's told don't refresh the airline app anymore. They walk straight to the belt.\n\nBuy 3 Get 2 Free. Free wireless charger. Free shipping. Link below. 👇",
